  "finding": [
    "At 998 tokens the floor is 24-32 splits (0.026 ms per call) and 48 splits costs 0.032 ms, so the plan's two-blocks-per-unit bound sits at the floor rather than a fourth wave.",
    "At 128 tokens the plan lands within 0.2% of the floor; the MIN_CHUNK bound keeps it from splitting a short context into blocks of two or three tokens.",
    "At 4098 tokens the plan reaches the 64-split cap and costs 0.062 ms against the 0.056 ms floor at 48, 11% over, on a call that is 2% of the step.",
    "Plan policy is unit-tested for 40, 96, 128, 2 and unknown compute-unit counts in tests/test_unit_yue2_attention_splitk.py."
  ],
  "rollback": "attention_route=\"strict\" selects the parent vv_attention_spans kernel."
